  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-23: "continue with other tasks so we can make progress". Issue #2982 (DI-162, filed by ebilling-r1 as ISS-044; read it in full). `SignalClosureService.ReadPoliciesNotInForceAsync` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalClosureService.cs` ~200-216) reads Off and Inactive policies with one unpaged `RetrieveMultipleAsync` per condition and ignores `MoreRecords`; `SignalReevaluationJob.ClosePoliciesNotInForceAsync` then closes open Signals per policy. Past 5,000 not-in-force policies the rest are silently skipped. ebilling task 117 switches record rules Off on every core-record delete, so the count grows.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, Dataverse SDK paging, ADR-036 scheduled jobs.</role>
  <goal>The close reads every not-in-force policy via id-cursor paging (copy `SecureChildReconciliationJob.cs` ~1384), dedupes across the two conditions, and logs/reports a truncated or failed read loudly (D-78: fail loudly and retry), so no open Signal of an Off/Inactive policy is silently left open.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Read the current SignalClosureService and SignalReevaluationJob on origin/master first (`git log -5` on both). Consider (only if cheap and correct) limiting the policy read to policies that still have open Signals; otherwise keep the per-policy close as is. Do not change which policies count as not in force, the close semantics (D-120 resolvedon = lastevaluated), or D-61 (never stamp unchanged Signals).</background>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">D-61, D-120, D-170 semantics unchanged; only completeness of the read and reporting change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §10">BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs fresh master (short paths, same zip tool, file counts) in the PR; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project CLAUDE.md §6">Filtered BFF tests only (never the unfiltered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests); full ArchTests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests: more than one page of policies are all closed (fails on origin/master); a page read failure is reported and not swallowed; Off and Inactive overlap is deduped.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Failing test: a fake returning MoreRecords across pages; policies on page 2 get their Signals closed.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement id-cursor paging; report truncation/failure (log + job outcome per D-78).</step>
    <step order="3">Filtered tests (SignalClosure, SignalReevaluation), full ArchTests, BFF build, publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="4">PR to master; notes in notes/task-204-notes.md; tell ebilling-r1 (they filed it) when merged.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Policies beyond the first page are read and their open Signals closed; test fails on origin/master.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A failed or truncated read is logged at Warning/Error with counts and surfaces as a job failure or a reported outcome, never a silent partial success.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Existing SignalClosure/SignalReevaluation tests pass unmodified; build, full ArchTests pass; publish-size delta reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>The fix needs a schema change, a new scheduled job, or changes which policies are closed: STOP and report.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <execution>
    <protocol>Run through task-execute. Fresh branch from origin/master in a short-path worktree; PR to master.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
